simio — third-party attribution

`src/sched.zig`, functions `entry` and `initialContext`: the naked fiber entry
trampoline (its three per-architecture instruction sequences) and the initial
stack-pointer layout it relies on (x86_64 `rsp = slot - 8`, aarch64/riscv64
`sp = slot`) are taken from the Zig standard library's `lib/std/Io/Uring.zig`
from Zig 0.16.0 (sha256
960efaa8fefd4e146929acfb45018db9f4bfd0ad331560e8e7bb0304889aec1b),
`AsyncClosure.entry` and `concurrent`, SOURCE, adapted: the trampoline hands
`fiberMain` a slot holding a `*Fiber` instead of an `AsyncClosure`. Nothing
else in this module is copied; the scheduler, wait bookkeeping, groups,
cancelation and time model are this collection's own. Zig's license follows
and must travel with those lines.

